<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francis II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">abdicated <a href="/years/1806">1806</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Emperor Francis II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francis II was the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a>. Faced with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s dominance, he proclaimed himself Emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> in 1804 and abdicated the Holy Roman imperial title in 1806, formally dissolving the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>. He continued to rule as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i">Francis I</a> of Austria.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Austrian Empire was proclaimed by <b>Francis II</b>, the last Holy Roman Emperor, on 11 August 1804.</blockquote><a href="/empire/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>At the Treaty of Campo Formio in 1797 <b>Francis II</b> gave up the Austrian Netherlands and Lombardy in return for Venice, and after defeats at Marengo and Hohenlinden in 1800 the Treaty of Lunéville of 1801 confirmed French control of the left bank of the Rhine and set…</blockquote><a href="/empire/habsburg-monarchy">Habsburg Monarchy · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Emperor Francis II</b>, who had already proclaimed himself Emperor of Austria in 1804, abdicated and declared the Holy Roman Empire dissolved on 6 August 1806, ending an institution that had claimed continuity for a thousand years.</blockquote><a href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>King <b>Francis II</b> withdrew to the fortified port of Gaeta and surrendered after the Siege of Gaeta in February 1861.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-two-sicilies">Kingdom of the Two Sicilies · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1806 Napoleon’s victories at Jena and Auerstedt broke the Prussian army, French troops entered Berlin, and the Holy Roman Empire had already been dissolved on 6 August 1806 when <b>Francis II</b> laid down the imperial crown, so that the electoral title lost its meaning.</blockquote><a href="/empire/margraviate-of-brandenburg">Margraviate of Brandenburg · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The melody is Joseph Haydn's, written in 1797 for Lorenz Leopold Haschka's &quot;Gott erhalte Franz den Kaiser&quot;, a birthday anthem for <b>Emperor Francis II</b> modelled on Britain's &quot;God Save the King&quot;.</blockquote><a href="/songs/deutschlandlied">Deutschlandlied</a></li></ul></section>
